   "hypothesis": "Hydra-NG = a deeper, narrower Full Attention Residuals + Canon trunk (27 blocks, FFN 4608 instead of the calibrated 23 x 6144 at equal FLOPs) with a hashed n-gram embedding memory read as an extra depth source. Closest prior methods: (a) attnres_full_canon_abcd (Kimi Block AttnRes with one group per block, i.e. Full AttnRes, plus Allen-Zhu Canon layers A-D), whose trunk and shell this keeps unchanged; (b) Over-Tokenized Transformer over-encoding (Huang et al. 2025) and DeepSeek Engram conditional memory (2026), which add hashed n-gram embedding tables; (c) nanochat/ResFormer value embeddings (kept). Difference: hashed bigram and trigram embeddings (two hash heads per order with distinct prime table sizes, about 335M lookup parameters in total) are concatenated, RMS-normalized and projected to the model width by one Muon-trained matrix; the result is not added to the input embedding or gated into a fixed layer, but becomes an additional source in the AttnRes depth attention, so every sublayer's pseudo-query and the final readout can weight the n-gram memory per token. The memory is causal (tokens t-n+1..t, row-start padding), adds ~0.2% FLOPs/token, and its tables are AdamW embedding parameters (value_embeds namespace). The source also contains a disabled mixture-of-experts FFN option (moe_experts=0)."
  }
